1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,920
Meet HybridPay — a universal fiat and crypto payment terminal.

2
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:16,720
One sandbox for banks, wallets, and smart contracts, where deterministic backend rules authorize every movement, and everything is audited.

3
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:23,740
The Banking Workspace shows live KPIs, programmable contracts, disputes, and an admin-gated control plane.

4
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:29,030
Operators read; money movement needs an admin token plus maker-checker approval.

5
00:00:29,030 --> 00:00:37,370
In the Personal Workspace I sign in with an operator token that lives only in browser memory, then send one thousand minor units.

6
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:41,440
Create, then confirm: the provider decides, never the frontend.

7
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:50,990
The simulator proves failures are first-class: a declined payment returns a structured provider decline, recorded as scenario passed, payment declined.

8
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:55,790
Timeouts stay ambiguous, contracts validate — never confused with an outage.

9
00:00:55,790 --> 00:01:03,340
Money with conditions: a plain-words agreement becomes a validated programmable contract, activated by its creator.

10
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:08,390
Guardrails never sleep — unknown categories rejected, wrong networks refused.

11
00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:12,400
The Meta Muse Spark integration advises only — never authorizes.

12
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:21,060
Every answer arrives labeled advisory-only; here it runs as a transparent sandbox stub, while real keys stay server-side in Modal Secrets.

13
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:27,250
History is tenant-isolated and searchable, with downloadable sandbox receipts for every record.

14
00:01:27,250 --> 00:01:33,630
The Private Workspace mirrors banking sign-in: role badges, tenant context, and a health-checked backend.

15
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:41,530
Receiving is Sepolia-only: a tracked request is created, and your own wallet signs — the terminal never sees keys.

16
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:44,160
Sandbox today, trusted rails tomorrow.
